    "response": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef score(item, bins):\n    residual = (bins - item)\n    distance_2 = (residual - 18.0)\n    product_3 = (distance_2 * distance_2)\n    negative_penalty_4 = -(product_3)\n    adjustment_5 = (bins + 1.0)\n    normalized_penalty_6 = (negative_penalty_4 / adjustment_5)\n    \n    # Reduce the number of bins used\n    # Here, we assume bins are sorted in ascending order and we only keep the first k bins\n    # where k is the smallest integer such that the sum of the remaining bins is at least 100\n    k = 1\n    while k < len(bins) and np.sum(bins[k:]) < 100:\n        k += 1\n    \n    # Select the highest score from the first k bins\n    max_score = np.max(normalized_penalty_6[:k])\n    return np.full_like(bins[:k], max_score)\n```",
